# SMTP Settings for Email Notifications
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=ntkdung1206@gmail.com

# Gemini API Credentials
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Security Encryption Key
ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (Postgres) — dùng làm database dùng chung, thay cho việc lưu
# src/db_store.json trực tiếp trong repo. Lấy 2 giá trị này tại:
# Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API.
#
# QUAN TRỌNG: đây là biến phía SERVER (không có tiền tố VITE_), nên KHÔNG
# bao giờ bị nhúng vào file JS công khai của trình duyệt. Dùng
# SERVICE_ROLE key (không phải anon key) vì server cần toàn quyền đọc/ghi
# và tự quản lý việc phân quyền Admin/Editor/Viewer ở tầng ứng dụng.
# Tuyệt đối không thêm tiền tố VITE_ vào 2 biến này.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing secret (src/server/auth.ts). Used to HMAC-sign the login
# session token issued by POST /api/login. Set this to a long random string
# in .env.local (and in Vercel Environment Variables for production) — anyone
# who knows this value can forge a valid Admin session, so treat it as a
# secret exactly like SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Protects GET /api/cron/weekly-backup (route name is legacy — it now runs
# the daily Google Drive database backup, see src/server/driveBackup.ts and
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID below; the email-based backup this route was
# originally named after was removed 2026-08-26) from being triggered by
# anyone who finds the URL. Vercel automatically sends
# `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` on its own Cron requests whenever
# this env var is set on the project — set it ONLY in Vercel Environment
# Variables (production). Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CRON_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — Facebook App credentials, used only to inspect how long a stored
# Page Access Token still has left (Graph API debug_token, see
# facebookSync.ts's fetchTokenExpiry). Leave both empty and the check falls
# back to inspecting each token with itself, which works for Page tokens; set
# them if you'd rather use the officially-documented App token instead. They
# are NOT needed to sync data — Page Access Tokens are pasted per page in
# Control Panel → Kết nối nền tảng → Facebook.
# Find them at developers.facebook.com → your App → Settings → Basic.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
FB_APP_ID=
FB_APP_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TikTok organic insights (src/server/tiktokSync.ts) — the TikTok half of the
# "Social Report" tab. Requires a TikTok Developer app with the Login Kit
# product added: https://developers.tiktok.com/apps
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Create an app at developers.tiktok.com/apps (or use an existing one).
#   2. Add the "Login Kit" product to the app.
#   3. Under Login Kit settings, add a Redirect URI — for local dev:
#        http://localhost:3000/api/tiktok/oauth/callback
#      for production, use your real domain instead of localhost:3000. That
#      exact string (scheme+host+path, no trailing slash) is TIKTOK_REDIRECT_URI
#      below — TikTok rejects the callback if it doesn't match exactly.
#   4. Request these scopes for the app: user.info.basic, user.info.stats,
#      video.list. Sandbox/test-user accounts can use them immediately;
#      real accounts need TikTok's App Review to be cleared first — this can
#      take TikTok some time to approve and isn't something this app can
#      shortcut, so kick it off early rather than only right before you need
#      the real connection.
#   5. Copy Client Key / Client Secret from the app's Basic Information page.
#
# Client Key is not secret on its own (it's sent to the browser as part of
# the authorize URL), but Client Secret is — treat it like
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=
TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=
TIKTOK_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/tiktok/oauth/callback

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YouTube organic insights (src/server/youtubeSync.ts) — the YouTube half of
# the "Social Report" tab (subscriber/view counts + per-video organic vs.
# advertising-driven views). Requires a Google Cloud OAuth Client ID:
# console.cloud.google.com
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Create (or reuse) a project at console.cloud.google.com.
#   2. APIs & Services > Library — enable "YouTube Data API v3" and
#      "YouTube Analytics API".
#   3. APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen — if the Google account is
#      part of Livotec/Karofi's Google Workspace, set User Type to
#      "Internal": skips Google's review entirely for these restricted
#      scopes and avoids the 7-day refresh_token expiry that "Testing"
#      status (External) apps get. Otherwise use External + Testing and add
#      the connecting Google account as a test user.
#   4. APIs & Services > Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID
#      > Web application. Add an Authorized redirect URI — for local dev:
#        http://localhost:3000/api/youtube/oauth/callback
#      for production, use your real domain instead of localhost:3000. That
#      exact string is YOUTUBE_REDIRECT_URI below — Google rejects the
#      callback if it doesn't match exactly.
#   5. Copy Client ID / Client Secret from the created OAuth client.
#   6. The Google account used to connect a channel needs at least
#      "Manager" role on that channel (YouTube Studio > Settings >
#      Permissions, if it's a Brand Account with multiple managers) —
#      "Communications Manager" is NOT enough, it can't use the API.
#
# Client ID is not secret on its own, but Client Secret is — treat it like
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=
YOUTUBE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/youtube/oauth/callback

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Ads paid campaign API (src/server/paidAdsApiSync.ts) — đồng bộ số
# liệu quảng cáo Google vào Digital Ads Report > Google. Requires:
#   - Google Ads API enabled in Google Cloud.
#   - OAuth client ID type "Web application" with redirect URI:
#       http://localhost:3000/api/google-ads/oauth/callback
#   - Google Ads Developer Token from Google Ads Manager > API Center.
#   - The Google account used in Control Panel must have access to the target
#     Customer ID (and, if using an MCC, enter that Manager ID in the UI).
# Scope requested by the app: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords
#
# Developer Token / Client Secret are server-only secrets. Never add VITE_.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_ADS_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/google-ads/oauth/callback
GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Drive full-database backup (src/server/driveBackup.ts) — the real
# "pg_dump equivalent" this app never had: the existing weekly email backup
# only ever covered the original report tables, never fb_pages/tiktok_*/
# youtube_*/ads_performance/audit logs etc. Runs daily, uploads a JSON dump
# of every table in supabase/schema.sql to a Google Drive folder.
#
# Deliberately a SEPARATE Google Cloud OAuth Client from YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID/
# SECRET above — this way a problem with that project (publish status,
# expiry, review) never takes down backups too. That said, you CAN reuse the
# exact same Google Cloud project/OAuth Client as YouTube if you'd rather
# not set up a second one: just add scope
# https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file and
# https://www.googleapis.com/auth/userinfo.email to that same OAuth consent
# screen, add one more Authorized redirect URI to that same Client, and use
# its Client ID/Secret for both sets of env vars below.
#
# Setup steps (same Google Cloud Console flow as YouTube above):
#   1. console.cloud.google.com — enable "Google Drive API".
#   2. OAuth consent screen — Internal if this is a Workspace-owned project
#      (same reasoning as YouTube: skips Google's review, no 7-day expiry).
#   3. Add scopes: drive.file, userinfo.email.
#   4. Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID > Web application.
#      Add an Authorized redirect URI — for local dev:
#        http://localhost:3000/api/backup/drive/oauth/callback
#      for production, use your real domain instead of localhost:3000.
#   5. Copy Client ID / Client Secret.
#   6. In the app: Control Panel > Sao Lưu Tự Động > "Kết nối Google Drive" —
#      pick which Google account/Drive the backups land in. Optionally paste
#      a Drive folder ID (open the folder in Drive, copy the ID from the URL)
#      to keep backups out of the root; leave blank to upload to Drive root.
#
# Client ID is not secret on its own, but Client Secret is — treat it like
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/backup/drive/oauth/callback

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telegram push notification (src/server/telegramNotifier.ts +
# expiryNotifier.ts) — pushes the "token sắp hết hạn" warning that Control
# Panel → "Kết nối nền tảng" already shows in-app (Facebook 7 ngày / TikTok
# 30 ngày / YouTube 2 ngày trước hạn) out to a Telegram chat, so the team
# finds out even when nobody has the Control Panel open. Runs once daily as
# part of GET /api/cron/facebook-sync (see vercel.json) — no extra cron entry
# needed. Chosen over WhatsApp Business Cloud API for setup simplicity: no
# Meta Business verification, no phone number, no pre-approved message
# template.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. In Telegram, message @BotFather → /newbot → follow the prompts → copy
#      the bot token it gives you (looks like 123456789:AAxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx).
#   2. Add the new bot to the group/channel that should receive alerts (or
#      just open a DM with it), then send it any message.
#   3. Get the chat ID: open
#      https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates in a browser (with your
#      real bot token) right after step 2 — look for "chat":{"id": ...} in
#      the JSON response. For a group chat this is usually a negative number.
#
# Bot token is effectively a password (whoever has it can post as this bot) —
# treat it like SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, never commit a real value.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
